;SAWTOO: PLEASE TYPE IN YOUR NAME:$
*T ==> "sawtoo" sawtooth recognizer program
*T     tool works by smoothing the input data and looking at the
*T     residue R = f-fsmooth.  A correlation convolution, based on
*T     an ideal sawtooth shape, is applied to the residue, resulting
*T     in a correlation function.  The sawtooth times are identified
*T     by picking off the peaks of the correlation function.
*T     Successful use of this program requires some skill...
*T     Missed sawteeth can be added by hand.
MCCUNE
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
H SAW MAX Q
;UFNTER:  ENTER OPCODE (D/E/F/P/S/Q... ):$
H SAW TIMES Q
;SAWTOO: ENTER 5 DIGIT SHOT #, "0" TO QUIT, "D" TO CHANGE NAMES$
89586
;SAWTOO:  ENTER OPTION CODE:$
G N
;SAWTOO:  ENTER OPTION CODE:$
S
; SUB:USMOO1 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
3
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
1 1.1 0
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
1 1.15 .025
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
1 2 .1
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
5
; SUB:USMOO1 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
10
; USMOO1:  ENTER "Y" TO PLOT DELTA(FINAL):$
N
; SUB:USMOO1 >> ENTER OPTION #:$
11
;SAWCOR:  ENTER MULTIPLICATIVE FACTOR FOR DELTA:$
,
;SAWCOR:  ENTER MINIMUM CORRELATION DELTA (seconds):$
,
;SAWCOR:  SPECIFY DATA/PLOT OPTION:$
4
;GRAOPT:  ENTER ONE LETTER OPCODE (.C/A/S/X/Z/G/P/Q):$
X 1.1 1.5
;GRAOPT:  ENTER ONE LETTER OPCODE (.C/A/S/X/Z/G/P/Q):$
N
;SAWCOR:  SPECIFY DATA/PLOT OPTION:$
S
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
1 1 .08
; SUB:PCIDEF >> ENTER OPTION #:$
5
;SAWCOR:  ENTER MINIMUM EVENT SEPERATION FACTOR (* DELTA(SM)):$
.1
;SAWCOR:  SPECIFY DATA/PLOT OPTION:$
P
;GRAOPT:  ENTER ONE LETTER OPCODE (.C/A/S/X/Z/G/P/Q):$
X 1.1 1.4
;GRAOPT:  ENTER ONE LETTER OPCODE (.C/A/S/X/Z/G/P/Q):$
Q
;SAWCOR:  SPECIFY DATA/PLOT OPTION:$
R
;SAWTOO:  ENTER OPTION CODE:$
X
